            <ArticleTitle>An introduction to the basic principles of health economics for those involved in the development and delivery of headache care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>709-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Against a background of increasing demands on limited resources, health economics is gaining an increasing impact on decision making and a basic understanding of the subject is important for all those involved in headache research and service delivery at whatever level. This paper is not intended as a review of the literature in the area of headache economics but discusses some general principles of health economics from the perspective of headache, with a focus on cost of illness studies and economic evaluation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
